---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { contactEmail, placeholders } from '../../site.config.mjs';
---
<Base
  title="Privacy Policy | Zenlingo"
  description="How Zenlingo handles your account, photos, lessons and purchases. Draft, pending legal review."
  path="/privacy/"
>
  <section class="page-title">
    <div class="wrap prose">
      <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="pending">Draft, pending legal review. This page is not final and must not be published as the final policy until reviewed.</p>

      <h2>Who we are</h2>
      <p>Zenlingo is operated by {placeholders.legalEntity}</p>

      <h2>What we collect</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Account.</strong> The identifier and details that Sign in with Apple provides, managed through our authentication service (Supabase Auth).</li>
        <li><strong>Photos.</strong> After you explicitly allow photo processing in the app, the photo you choose is sent to OpenAI to create a lesson. We store a reduced copy of the photo in Supabase with your collection. We do not keep original-resolution photos. Your originals stay in your photo library.</li>
        <li><strong>Lessons and practice.</strong> The lessons, expressions, questions and answers that the app saves. Your latest completed full-lesson result is stored only on your iPhone.</li>
        <li><strong>Settings.</strong> Your chosen English level.</li>
        <li><strong>Purchases.</strong> Subscription status, handled through Apple and RevenueCat. We do not receive your payment card details.</li>
        <li><strong>Audio.</strong> Pronunciation audio is produced on your iPhone by the built-in iOS speech voice. The words are not sent to any third party for audio.</li>
        <li><strong>Product analytics.</strong> The app sends a small set of anonymous usage events (for example that a photo was chosen, a lesson was completed or a subscription screen was viewed) to PostHog, hosted in the EU. Events use a random ID created on your iPhone that is not linked to your account, Apple ID, email or purchases, and is replaced when you sign out or delete your account. They never contain your photos, lesson content, answers or location, and we do not use advertising identifiers or tracking.</li>
        <li><strong>Advertising.</strong> The app does not include advertising tools.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Zenlingo does not record your voice, use speech recognition or score pronunciation.</p>

      <h2>How we use this information</h2>
      <p>To create lessons from your photos, save and sync your collection, check your access, show your results, and respond to support requests.</p>

      <h2>Service providers</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Apple (Sign in with Apple, App Store purchases)</li>
        <li>OpenAI (photo processing to create lessons)</li>
        <li>Supabase (authentication, storage of your collection and reduced photos)</li>
        <li>RevenueCat (purchase status)</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>How long we keep data</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>While your account is active, your collection stays in the cloud.</li>
        <li>After your access ends, we keep your cloud collection for 90 days. Renewing within that time restores access to it. After 90 days we delete it.</li>
        <li>If you delete your account, we block it immediately and delete your account and learning data from active systems within seven days. There is no recovery period.</li>
        <li>Backups are kept isolated until they expire. Backups are encrypted and expire on a rolling basis, within 7 days. Deleted data is not restored into active systems.</li>
        <li>Lessons and results stored on your iPhone are removed when you delete a lesson, sign out or delete your account.</li>
        <li><strong>Free-lesson marker.</strong> Account deletion previously kept a one-way marker: an HMAC-SHA256 keyed hash of your Apple account identifier, made with a secret server key. It held no Apple ID, name or email, and it was no longer linked to your account. It also kept the request keys tried and the delivery time. Its only purpose was to stop the free first lesson from being claimed twice. We removed it on 2026-10-20 when the free lesson was retired, and we no longer keep it. [Draft, pending legal review.]</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Your choices</h2>
      <p>You can stop allowing photo processing in Account at any time; this does not delete lessons already saved. You can delete a lesson in the app, or delete your account from Account. Deleting your account does not cancel an Apple subscription. Cancel it in your Apple subscription settings.</p>

      <h2>Children</h2>
      <p>Zenlingo is for people aged 13 and over, and you need an Apple Account to sign in. It is not directed to children under 13, and we do not knowingly collect their data. If you are under the age of majority where you live, use Zenlingo only with a parent or guardian's permission. If you believe a child has given us data, write to us and we will delete it.</p>

      <h2>International transfers</h2>
      <p>Our service providers (Apple, OpenAI, Supabase, RevenueCat and PostHog) may process data in countries other than yours. Your collection and account data are hosted by Supabase in Canada, photo processing by OpenAI and purchase status by RevenueCat may take place in the United States, and PostHog analytics are hosted in the EU. When your data leaves your country we rely on the safeguards the law allows, such as standard contractual clauses or the adequacy decisions that apply to those providers. Contact us for a copy of the safeguards that apply to you.</p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>Controller: Ricardo Gusman Brandão, an individual developer based in Brazil. Questions, access, correction, portability, objection or deletion requests: <a href={`mailto:${contactEmail}`}>{contactEmail}</a>. You may also have the right to complain to your data protection authority, such as the ANPD in Brazil. We reply within 15 days.</p>

      <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
      <p>If we change this policy in a material way, we will tell you in the app or by email before the change takes effect, and we will update the date on this page. Where the law requires your consent for a new use, we will ask for it.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
